# Chip Estimate Integrity — Phase F: Calibration persistence (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (validator-remediated before the follow-up implementation edit)
# F1 GIVEN a persisted booked-vendor `book_movers` response, WHEN moving-day
#    check-in loads, THEN the stored vendor, estimated low/high range,
#    and move scope can be parsed; the form shows one optional final-bill money
#    field. GIVEN no booked vendor (including quote-only or malformed stored
#    responses), THEN the final-bill question is not rendered or submitted.
#    JSON booleans are never accepted as numeric low/high/cubicFeet/driveMinutes.
# F2 GIVEN a signed-in check-in submission, WHEN `submitCheckIn` runs, THEN it
#    validates the four existing factual answers and an optional positive,
#    finite final bill, re-reads `users/{uid}/workflowResponses/book_movers`,
#    and derives vendor, estimate, and scope only from that server-side read;
#    vendor/estimate/scope injected into the same check-in request cannot
#    influence calibration. The existing stored booking remains the source.
# F3 GIVEN a booked vendor and valid final bill, WHEN the review is accepted,
#    THEN one atomic server-side operation writes the existing review plus a new
#    top-level `estimateCalibration/{autoId}` document containing reviewId,
#    userId, vendorId, estimatedRange, finalBill, scopeSnapshot, and submittedAt.
#    Omitted final bill or no booked vendor writes no estimate-calibration doc.
# F4 GIVEN Firestore access control, WHEN Phase F ships, THEN
#    `estimateCalibration` remains backend-owned: no client write path and no
#    Firestore rule granting client access is added. `firestore.rules` is not
#    changed.
# F5 GIVEN a box-return submission, WHEN calibration is saved and read back,
#    THEN `users/{uid}.kitCalibration` retains delivered and returned counts and
#    also round-trips the user's `ranOut` yes/no answer. Its UI requires that
#    answer and keeps pickup behavior unchanged.
# F6 GIVEN the complete Phase F change, WHEN verification runs, THEN focused
#    Node and Swift unit tests, booked/unbooked UI coverage, signed live
#    persistence readback, fresh validation, and walked diffs pass. Only
#    `functions:submitCheckIn` is deployed; no rule deploy or flow reseed occurs.
#
